<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sudanese Union – African Democratic Rally</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as US-RDA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sudanese Union – <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rassemblement-democratique-africain">African Democratic Rally</a> (US-RDA) was a political party in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, founded in 1946 as the local section of the African Democratic Rally. Led by Mamadou Konaté and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modibo-keita">Modibo Keïta</a>, it won the elections of the 1950s, led the territory to autonomy as the Sudanese Republic in 1958 and to independence in 1960, and ruled Mali as its single party until the coup of 1968.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sudanese-union-african-democratic-rally.jpg" alt="Sudanese Union – African Democratic Rally" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown , vectorized by Perhelion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Mali.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
